# Step 1.1 — authentication. Run `bun run dev`, then use VS Code "REST Client"
# (humao.rest-client); it keeps cookies between requests, like a browser.
# Better Auth's own routes (/api/auth/*) answer in Better Auth's format, not our envelope.
@base = http://localhost:3000
@origin = http://localhost:3000

### Sign up (signs in immediately → Set-Cookie: better-auth.session_token)
POST {{base}}/api/auth/sign-up/email
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{origin}}

{ "name": "  Asha Rao  ", "email": "Asha@Example.com", "password": "correct-horse-battery" }

### Trying to self-assign ADMIN is ignored → role stays USER
POST {{base}}/api/auth/sign-up/email
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{origin}}

{ "name": "Mallory", "email": "mallory@example.com", "password": "correct-horse-battery", "role": "ADMIN" }

### Same email, different case → rejected
POST {{base}}/api/auth/sign-up/email
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{origin}}

{ "name": "Asha Again", "email": "ASHA@example.com", "password": "correct-horse-battery" }

### Wrong password → 401 (generic message)
POST {{base}}/api/auth/sign-in/email
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{origin}}

{ "email": "asha@example.com", "password": "wrong-password" }

### Sign in
POST {{base}}/api/auth/sign-in/email
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{origin}}

{ "email": "asha@example.com", "password": "correct-horse-battery" }

### Current session (null when signed out)
GET {{base}}/api/auth/get-session

### Our endpoint guarded by requireUser → 200 signed in, 401 (our envelope) signed out
GET {{base}}/api/dev/probe/whoami

### requireAdmin → 403 for USER. Promote for testing (until the step 1.2 CLI):
###   docker compose exec postgres psql -U hacker -d hacker_house -c "UPDATE users SET role='ADMIN' WHERE email='asha@example.com'"
GET {{base}}/api/dev/probe/admin-only

### Disabled endpoint → 404
POST {{base}}/api/auth/update-user
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{origin}}

{ "name": "New Name" }

### Foreign Origin → rejected by Better Auth's origin check
POST {{base}}/api/auth/sign-in/email
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: https://evil.example

{ "email": "asha@example.com", "password": "correct-horse-battery" }

### Sign out (deletes the session row; the old cookie stops working).
### Better Auth requires a JSON content type on every POST, even without a body.
POST {{base}}/api/auth/sign-out
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{origin}}

{}
